    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_c5042def",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a Black man restrained in a chair by multiple white men, with overlaid text claiming that 'they don't know how to use condom' and 'this is the only way to control their population.' This juxtaposition of a degrading, coercive visual with racist text constitutes a hateful message. It uses the visual of forced restraint to symbolize population control, directly targeting Black people with a racist and dehumanizing stereotype rooted in historical eugenics and racialized medical experimentation. The meme promotes a harmful and hateful narrative that justifies systemic oppression and control over Black communities through the false premise of 'population control' and the hypersexualization of Black men, which is a known anti-Black stereotype. The intent is to incite racial hatred and reinforce racist ideologies by equating Black people with biological inferiority and the need for state-imposed control.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_14814973"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
